1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:03,367
The Fed cuts rates. Your mortgage payment? Still

2
00:00:03,367 --> 00:00:04,142
the same.

3
00:00:04,600 --> 00:00:07,467
For a standard U.S. fixed-rate mortgage, you signed

4
00:00:07,467 --> 00:00:09,975
a contract with a set interest rate.

5
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:13,369
That rate does not reset when the Fed

6
00:00:13,369 --> 00:00:15,225
changes its overnight lending target.

7
00:00:15,667 --> 00:00:19,612
Your scheduled principal-and-interest payment stays flat, even if

8
00:00:19,612 --> 00:00:21,092
market rates fall.

9
00:00:21,533 --> 00:00:24,790
Refinancing replaces that old mortgage with a new

10
00:00:24,790 --> 00:00:27,233
loan. It is a separate decision,

11
00:00:27,667 --> 00:00:30,667
with approval, closing costs, and a new term

12
00:00:30,667 --> 00:00:31,417
to compare.

13
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:35,067
One catch: taxes and insurance can still change

14
00:00:35,067 --> 00:00:36,667
your total monthly bill.

15
00:00:37,067 --> 00:00:40,017
A rate cut changes the backdrop. It does

16
00:00:40,017 --> 00:00:41,492
not rewrite your contract.
